  "notes": [
    "Venue frame: metres, x east, y north. Directions are compass bearings in degrees. Schema: docs/venue-file.md.",
    "Fictional (#36). Pairings name the version-7 conditions files (schema 6, finite pressure lanes, #303); schema 2 so the geography shapes the pressure field (ADR 0008).",
    "Each pairing's geographic grid is laid square to its mean wind: 100 m cells, 500 m either side of the start line centre, from 300 m below it to 700 m above, which covers the race area at the seeded mean's full ±10° with a 360 m beat.",
    "Land lies beyond the race area at every seeded mean, at least 30 m clear of it, for the largest fleet and the longest beat: the offline venue check (VenueCheck, #83) and the sailability check (VenueSailability) pass for every pairing.",
    "Hill-ringed lake (#12): land all round, clear of the race area, no current (#11). The hills are relief for the chart (#115), not landmarks.",
    "The land is four pieces meeting on the lake's diagonals: one ring of shore, written as four simple polygons.",
    "Strong geographic shifts and land shadow: the wind bends round the hills and comes through the gaps.",
    "Light and patchy from 200, across the lake from the low ground in the south-south-west: a lane of more pressure (up to 14 %) and lane spots down the course from the gap, shadow of up to 22 % under the higher shore either side of it, and the wind bending up to 8 deg round the western hills.",
    "Gusty offshore from 290, off the western hills: shadow of up to 25 % under them, a lane of more pressure from the valley at the west, and the wind bending up to 12 deg round the hills north and south of it.",
    "Geographic grids and side tendencies are placeholders until the bot suite and play teach what reads well."
  ],
